{
  "title": "catalog-clean-aliases drops aliases that prod's stored lines still need",
  "description": "make catalog-clean-aliases removes curated aliases the current parser no longer produces, judged against the committed corpora, which re-parse raw text. \
Prod never re-parses: lines keep the item as parsed at save. 0b877f902d removed \"katakuriko (potato starch\" and \"ribs celery (about 8 ounces\" (the parser now closes the paren), and 4 prod lines that counted at #825 are now \"No supported nutrition match\" (found by make ingredient-prod-report, run at #825 and at HEAD). \
Fix: have catalog-clean-aliases (and its test of produced names) also read PROD_RECIPES= and keep any alias a stored prod item still hits; restore the two aliases. \
Revisit once stored lines are re-parsed (blocked-apply-prod-burndown-fixes, D2). \
Offline catalog tooling only: no web or iOS change.",
